PART 2 — The Detection Layer: What People Say vs. What They Feel

2A. Defence mechanisms. Vaillant (1992, Ego Mechanisms of Defense; 1977 four-level hierarchy) — psychotic (delusional projection, denial, distortion), immature (acting out, passive aggression, dissociation, projection, fantasy, splitting, somatisation), neurotic (intellectualisation, displacement, reaction formation, repression, isolation of affect), mature (sublimation, altruism, suppression, humour, anticipation — mnemonic SASHA). Cramer (2015, "Defense mechanisms: 40 years of empirical research") and Tausczik & Pennebaker (2010) supply the linguistic-marker layer. For each mechanism define: clinical definition → Vaillant level → surface pattern (words, syntax, topic avoidance) → most-likely hidden emotion(s) with probability mapping → Gita-aligned bypass that does not confront the defence. 
